  "report_summary": "Bilateral staging breast MRI with IV gadolinium in a 66-year-old with biopsy-proven right breast invasive ductal carcinoma. Right breast shows a 52 x 44 x 38mm irregular avidly enhancing necrotic mass in the lower outer quadrant with frank dermal invasion (T4b, 9mm skin thickening) and extensive associated non-mass enhancement extending a further 28mm superiorly, giving approximately 80mm total disease extent; the posterior margin involves the pectoral fascia with pectoral muscle invasion not definitively excluded. Bulky multilevel right axillary nodal disease with a 32 x 28mm level 1 node showing complete cortical replacement and suspected extracapsular extension, level 2 nodes to 18mm and an indeterminate 12mm level 3 apical node (N2-3 clinically). Left breast normal and no internal mammary chain lymphadenopathy. Right MRI 6, left MRI 1. Advanced locoregional disease for urgent MDT discussion with primary systemic therapy recommended prior to surgery."
